/-!
# p-bases, differentials and intersections of subfields

Stacks Project, Chapter 15 "More on Algebra". The tags treated here are

07P1, 07P4, 07P5.

## Tag 07P1 — p-independent families and p-bases

For a field extension `K / k` and a natural number `p`, form the compositum in `K` of `k`
and the `p`-th powers in `K`. A family in `K` is p-independent over `k` when its monomials
whose exponents are strictly less than `p` are linearly independent over this compositum. It
is a p-basis when these monomials form a basis of `K` over the compositum.

### Main definitions

* `PIndependent`: p-independence of a family over a field.
* `PBasis`: the property that a family is a p-basis of a field extension.

### Main results

There are no results beyond the two definitions.

### Implementation notes

These predicates make sense without assuming that `p` is prime or that the fields have
characteristic `p`; later results impose those hypotheses. These are the
definitions shared with the development of the subsequent results about p-bases.

### References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07P1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07P1)

## Tag 07P4 — Directed intersections of subfields in positive characteristic

For a directed family of subfields of a field `K` whose intersection is the subfield of
`p`-th powers, the corresponding maps on Kähler differentials have kernels with trivial
intersection. The analogous intersection property persists after every finite extension of
`K`.

### Main definitions

There are no new definitions.

### Main results

* `iInf_ker_kaehlerDifferentialMap_eq_bot_and_frobeniusFieldRange_eq_iInf` gives
  both the assertion about Kähler differentials and its finite-extension counterpart.

### Implementation notes

The subfield of `p`-th powers is represented by the field range of Frobenius. The compositum
`L^p K_α` is represented by the supremum of this field range with the image of `K_α` in
`L`.

### References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07P4]

## Tag 07P5 — Subfields from power series rings and p-bases

Let `x` be a p-basis of a field `k` of characteristic `p`. For every finite set `J` of
indices, let `kJ` be generated by the p-th powers in `k` and the basis elements whose indices
are outside `J`. Replacing the coefficients by `kJ` and every power-series and polynomial
variable by its p-th power gives a subring `AJ` of
`k[[X₁, ..., Xₙ]][Y₁, ..., Yₘ]` and hence a subfield `KJ` of its fraction field.

### Main definitions

There are no new definitions.

### Main results

* `fractionFields_powerSeries_polynomial_subrings` states that the fields `KJ`
  contain all p-th powers, have intersection precisely the p-th powers, and are downward
  directed, and that every extension `AJ ⊆ A` is finite.

### Implementation notes

The ring `AJ` is represented as the range of the homomorphism from the corresponding power
series-polynomial ring over `kJ`. Its fraction field inside `Frac(A)` is the intermediate field
generated by the image of this range. This realizes the inclusions in the source canonically.

### References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07P5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07P5)

-/

